"requests":1},"project.portability":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1527.6666666666667,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":226.11111111111111,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":63777.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1757.0,"requests":4}}}},"discovery_journal":null,"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the 'supersede' terminology with the no-supersede decision — rename the AC/test to reflect append-once/no-conflicting-duplicate (e.g. test_breadcrumb_idempotent_no_second_on_ancestor_change) or add a note that 'supersede' here means 'suppress a second breadcrumb', not edit the original.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7614,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'This is append-once ... first-writer-wins'","'No supersede/edit of a stale breadcrumb'","AC: 'verified by test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_idempotent_and_supersede'"],"finding":"AC line 2 and its test are named '..._and_supersede', and the section heading is 'Append-once / supersede', but the plan explicitly states there is NO supersede (ADD-only, first-writer-wins, Accepted limitation). The 'supersede' terminology in the AC/test name describes behavior the plan deliberately does not implement.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff42b3313b72ff2ae","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 2 / heading 'Append-once / supersede'","norm_id":"nd1a7f01fa6143767","priority":0.1886,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concurrency assumption for the check-then-act dedup (serialized passes per child) or note the residual duplicate-on-race window, so the append-once claim is qualified accurately.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'before appending, scan the resolved jira_comments (normalized via _normalize_comment_body...) for the tag; if present, emit nothing'","'This is append-once and stable across passes'","ABSENCE: the plan does not state passes are serialized per child, and dedup is read-then-write against a per-pass snapshot/live fetch with no atomic guard"],"finding":"The append-once guarantee is a check-then-act (scan resolved jira_comments for the tag, then append if absent) that relies on each pass seeing the prior pass's posted comment. Two overlapping/concurrent passes over the same child could each read jira_comments before either posts, and both would append a breadcrumb — violating the stated first-writer-wins/append-once invariant.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd32b0a0588e8cf94","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Append-once / supersede' sectio